UPDATE stories
SET
  summary_compact = CASE story_key
    WHEN 'models' THEN 'A compact open-model release improves local planning and reasoning, narrowing the gap with larger systems while keeping capable AI available on-device.'
    WHEN 'agents' THEN 'Browsers are becoming the agent workspace as teams standardize dependable tool-use flows that can complete routine work across familiar web applications.'
    WHEN 'research' THEN 'New fine-tuning results show that carefully selected smaller datasets can improve model quality, reducing the cost and time needed for targeted training.'
    WHEN 'product' THEN 'Voice assistants are improving turn-taking and interruption handling, making spoken interactions feel less intrusive and more useful in everyday settings.'
    WHEN 'business' THEN 'Enterprise AI budgets are moving from experiments to inference as organizations measure production usage and prioritize systems that deliver ongoing value.'
  END,
  summary = CASE story_key
    WHEN 'models' THEN 'A compact open-model release brings stronger planning and reasoning to local devices, giving developers a practical option when privacy, latency, or deployment control matter. The update signals that capable reasoning is no longer limited to the largest hosted systems and may accelerate on-device AI products.'
    WHEN 'agents' THEN 'Browsers are becoming the new workspace for agents as tool use shifts from demonstrations toward dependable workflows inside familiar web applications. The change matters because browser-based agents can connect research, data entry, and operational tasks without forcing teams to adopt a separate interface for every automated process.'
    WHEN 'research' THEN 'Smaller, more carefully selected datasets are producing sharper fine-tuning results, showing that targeted examples can matter more than raw training volume. This can lower the cost of adapting models to specialized domains while helping teams focus on data quality, evaluation, and the specific behaviors they need to improve.'
    WHEN 'product' THEN 'Voice interfaces are learning when to stay quiet by improving turn-taking, interruption handling, and awareness of conversational pauses. Better timing can make assistants less intrusive in homes and workplaces, where a technically accurate response still feels unhelpful if it arrives at the wrong moment or cuts someone off.'
    WHEN 'business' THEN 'Enterprise AI spending is moving toward inference as companies replace experimental budgets with usage tied to real production workloads. The shift favors teams that can measure value per request, manage operating costs, and build reliable systems that continue delivering results after an initial pilot has ended.'
  END,
  summary_detailed = CASE story_key
    WHEN 'models' THEN 'A compact open-model release brings stronger planning and reasoning to local devices, narrowing the gap with much larger hosted systems. For developers, this creates a more credible path to private, low-latency AI features that can run close to users instead of sending every request to a remote service. The practical question is no longer only whether an open model can answer a prompt, but whether it can plan, use context, and complete multi-step work reliably enough for a product. Teams evaluating the release should compare quality on their own tasks, hardware requirements, and the cost of maintaining an on-device deployment.'
    WHEN 'agents' THEN 'Browsers are becoming the working surface for agents as tool use moves beyond demonstrations toward dependable workflows in familiar web applications. This matters because much of a knowledge worker''s routine work already happens in tabs: researching information, moving data between systems, completing forms, and checking outcomes. A browser-based agent can reduce context switching, but reliability remains the deciding factor. Teams should define clear boundaries for what an agent may do, require confirmation for consequential actions, and measure whether completed workflows are accurate, recoverable, and genuinely faster than the existing process.'
    WHEN 'research' THEN 'Smaller datasets can produce sharper fine-tuning when the examples are selected for relevance, quality, and coverage rather than sheer volume. The finding gives teams a useful alternative to collecting large, expensive corpora before adapting a model to a specialized workflow. It also shifts attention to dataset design: identifying the failures that matter, including representative edge cases, and evaluating whether the tuned model improves on those cases without losing broader capability. Organizations can use this approach to shorten iteration cycles, but should keep holdout evaluations and human review in place so apparent gains are not caused by narrow or contaminated training data.'
    WHEN 'product' THEN 'Voice interfaces are improving turn-taking by recognizing pauses, interruptions, and moments when silence is the better response. That capability affects product trust because conversational systems can feel intrusive even when their answers are correct if they interrupt, respond too quickly, or continue after a user has changed direction. Better timing can make assistants more natural in shared spaces and workplace settings where people often speak to each other rather than to the device. Product teams should evaluate these changes with realistic multi-person and noisy-environment scenarios, while retaining visible controls that let people pause, correct, or disengage the assistant.'
    WHEN 'business' THEN 'Enterprise AI budgets are moving from exploratory pilots toward inference spending as organizations track the actual use of systems in production. This is a meaningful maturity signal: leaders are increasingly asking whether each request, workflow, or customer interaction produces enough value to justify its ongoing operating cost. The change favors teams that can monitor latency, quality, adoption, and cost together instead of treating model selection as a one-time procurement decision. Companies scaling AI should establish cost ownership, set service-level expectations, and regularly compare automated outcomes with the baseline process so production growth remains economically sustainable.'
  END
WHERE edition_id = (SELECT id FROM editions WHERE edition_date = '2026-08-23')
  AND story_key IN ('models', 'agents', 'research', 'product', 'business');
